  <section class="prose col">
    <p class="lede">At 2:07 PM, your first coffee has already done its job.</p>
    <p>The problem is that the job is over.</p>
    <p>So you reach for another cup.</p>
    <p>Not because you are craving coffee. Because you want your afternoon back.</p>
    <figure>
      <img src="{{ 'lpi-crash-closeup.jpg' | asset_url }}" width="1024" height="768" alt="An empty coffee mug with a dried ring in sharp focus, a tired man resting his head on his hand blurred behind it">
      <figcaption>2:07 PM. The first cup is finished, and so is the lift it came with.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>The second coffee gets you moving again. Then the other stuff shows up.</p>
    <p>The jittery energy.</p>
    <p>The racing mind.</p>
    <p>The feeling that your body is switched on, but your brain is not doing better work.</p>
    <p>Now you are trying to solve one problem with the thing that created the next one.</p>
    <p class="punch">That is the<br class="m"> second-coffee loop.</p>
    <p>And it is why the third cup always seems to arrive faster than the first.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="col">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Does this sound familiar?</h2>
      <ul class="rows">
        <li><i><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 8h12v6a5 5 0 0 1-5 5H9a5 5 0 0 1-5-5z"/><path d="M16 10h2a2 2 0 0 1 0 4h-2"/><path d="M7 3v2M10 3v2M13 3v2"/></svg></i>Your first coffee works until early afternoon, then disappears all at once</li>
        <li><i><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 4h12l-1 16H7z"/><path d="M6 9h12"/><path d="M9 13h6"/></svg></i>You order the second cup because you need to function, not because you want the taste</li>
        <li><i><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M13 2 4 14h7l-1 8 9-12h-7z"/></svg></i>More caffeine makes you feel more switched on, but not more clear</li>
        <li><i><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="4" y="5" width="7" height="15" rx="1.5"/><rect x="13" y="8" width="7" height="12" rx="1.5"/><path d="M6 3h3M15 6h3"/></svg></i>You keep adding coffee or energy drinks because the last one stopped doing enough</li>
        <li><i><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 12h4l2-5 3 10 2-6 2 3h5"/></svg></i>You want energy that does not turn the rest of your body up with it</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="cost">
        <p>You reread the same email three times and it still does not go out.</p>
        <p>You are short with someone on the 3 PM call and can hear it while it is happening.</p>
        <p>You get home at 6 and the useful part of you is already spent.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="card__turn">The problem is not that you need more coffee.</p>
      <p>The problem is that you keep asking the same tool to create energy, erase fatigue, and carry you through the rest of the day.</p>
    </div>
