  <section class="sec prose col">
    <div class="num"><span class="num__n">2</span><h2>The push-pull problem</h2></div>
    <p>Caffeine gives you a temporary push, but it does not remove the tiredness underneath.</p>
    <p>By the second cup, you are stacking more stimulation on top of the fatigue that was already there. That is why you can feel wired and still struggle to focus.</p>
    <p class="big">It is not more energy. It is the same fatigue with the volume turned up around it.</p>
    <p>So the afternoon does not always need a stronger second cup. It needs a different kind of lift.</p>
    <ol class="pp" aria-label="How the push-pull problem builds">
      <li class="pp__s"><span class="pp__n">1</span><span class="pp__t">Tired at 2 PM</span><span class="pp__g"><i class="pp__base"></i></span></li>
      <li class="pp__a" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></li>
      <li class="pp__s"><span class="pp__n">2</span><span class="pp__t">Coffee creates a temporary push</span><span class="pp__g"><i class="pp__base"></i><i class="pp__push"></i></span></li>
      <li class="pp__a" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></li>
      <li class="pp__s"><span class="pp__n">3</span><span class="pp__t">Fatigue remains underneath</span><span class="pp__g"><i class="pp__base"></i><i class="pp__push pp__push--fading"></i></span></li>
      <li class="pp__a" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></li>
      <li class="pp__s pp__s--end"><span class="pp__n">4</span><span class="pp__t">More stimulation, less clarity</span><span class="pp__g"><i class="pp__base"></i><i class="pp__push"></i><i class="pp__push pp__push--2"></i><i class="pp__noise"></i></span></li>
    </ol>
    <p class="pp__cap">The push sits on top of the tiredness. It never replaces it.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="sec prose col">
    <div class="num"><span class="num__n">3</span><h2>More caffeine is still the same answer</h2></div>
    <p>Switch from coffee to an energy drink and the packaging changes.</p>
    <p>The afternoon strategy does not.</p>
    <p>You are still turning the same volume knob higher and hoping this time the result feels different.</p>
    <p>That is why the familiar alternatives do not feel like much of an escape:</p>
    <div class="card card--paper">
      <ul class="rows">
        <li><i><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><ellipse cx="12" cy="12" rx="6" ry="9" transform="rotate(-30 12 12)"/><path d="M8 17c3-3 5-6 8-10" transform="rotate(-30 12 12)"/></svg></i>Coffee with a different roast</li>
